<title>MEXICO: Mexico sets tariff-free milk import quota for 1997.</title>
<headline>Mexico sets tariff-free milk import quota for 1997.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico published Thursday the country's 1997 tariff-free import quotas for milk powder, giving the lion's share to the state-owned staples agency Conasupo.</p>
<p>Via the government's Official Gazettee, the Trade Ministry set a tariff-free import level of 43,709.1 tonnes, of which Conasupo was given a 43,587.7 tonne quota.</p>
<p>The remaining 121.4 tonnes will be awarded to milk power companies in the south of the country, including Quintana Roo and the states that border Guatemala, the ministry said.</p>
<p>((--Chris Aspin, Mexico City newsroom +525 7289530))</p>
